The wink. The lash-visible wink that worked this morning. It works again. The chat detonates. I hit End Stream before the dopamine wears off.

Duration: 1 hour 47 minutes
Peak Viewers: 339
Average Viewers: 206
New Followers: 34
Total Followers: 252
Donations: $186.00
Subscribers: 11

$186. In under two hours. At night. After already earning $177 this morning.

Day total (ElliePlayz): $363.00

I close OBS. Close VoxMorph. Take off the wig. The face returns. Eli. The person the numbers don't belong to. The person the viewers don't know about.

I open the RegenaForm app.

Not browsing this time. Calculating. The Tier 1 menu loads   every option, every price, every feature I haven't purchased yet. I scroll through them with the focused attention of a person planning a renovation, which is exactly what this is.

Current modifications:
- Eyelashes   Natural-Long (1.8a): FREE ✓
- Brow Sculpt   Feathered (1.7a): 300 $ (on credit, due in 5 days) ✓
- Wig   StreamLine: FREE ✓

Next target:
- Nose   Slope (1.5a): 500 $

The nose. The next piece. The slope nose would narrow the bridge, refine the tip, bring the nose from "slightly large and asymmetric" to "feminine and clean." It's the next step down from the eyes   the feature that sits between the visible zone and the hidden zone, the bridge between the face the viewers see and the face they don't.

With the nose done, the crop line could drop another inch. Show the nose. Show the bridge. Show more of the face while still hiding the jaw and lips. Incremental reveal. Each modification purchasing another inch of visibility. Each inch earning more.

The math:

Day 1 earnings (ElliePlayz): $210
Day 2 earnings (ElliePlayz): $363
Total ElliePlayz earnings: $504

Brow sculpt debt: 300 $ (due in 5 days)
$504 - $300 = $204 remaining after debt

Nose   Slope: 500 $
$204 short of nose cost: need $296 more

At current rate ($363/day average of Day 4): one more day of streaming covers the nose with surplus.

One day. One more day of being Ellie and the nose is paid for. And after the nose, the next feature   lips? Jawline? Cheekbones? Each one has a cost and each cost has a timeline and the timeline is measured in streams and the streams are measured in dollars and the dollars are real and the face is changing and the math works.

It all works. The system that Kira identified   the system that rewards a specific input   is producing exactly the output the math predicted. The loop is running. The escalation is functioning. The door opened and behind it is money and behind the money is a face and behind the face is a life.

I scroll the app further. Past Tier 1. Into the overview.

Tier 1   Facial Feminization: 500-4,500 $ total (partially complete)
Tier 2   Voice Modulation (organic): 1,200-3,500 $
Tier 3   Hair Redesign: 800-3,500 $
Tier 4   Body Contour: 3,000-8,000 $

The numbers are large. The tiers stretch upward like floors in a building, each one more expensive than the last, each one further from the starting point. But the starting point was $0 and $47 in the bank and now it's $504 in four days and the trajectory isn't slowing down, it's accelerating. Each modification improves the stream. Each improved stream generates more money. Each dollar funds the next modification. The loop is the product. The escalation is the business model.

I close the app.

I should tell Kira. Soon. Maybe after the nose. Once the face is one step further, once the investment is more concrete, once the numbers are undeniable   then I'll tell her. I'll sit her down and show her the dashboard and explain the logic: you told me the system rewards a specific input. I changed the input. Look at what happened.

She'll understand. She's Kira. She's pragmatic. She identified the problem.

And she's bisexual. The thought returns   the same rationalization from last night, polished smoother with repetition. She likes girls AND she likes me. A few feminine features on her boyfriend wouldn't repel her. It might attract her. The modified face   the lashes, the brows, eventually the nose and the lips   wouldn't push her away. It would add a dimension. Both sides of her attraction converging on the same person. She said it herself: "I like the way women look. I like softness." And I'm building softness onto a frame she already likes.

She won't mind. A bit of feminine on her boyfriend. She might even find it beautiful. She sees beauty in unusual places   in penguin anatomy facts at 4 AM, in a guy who sits still for 45 minutes so she can nap. She'd see beauty in this too.

I'll tell her. After the nose. After one more step.

The RegenaForm app glows on my phone. I set it beside the mattress, screen down.

[[Go to Sleep|day_4_26_kira]]

:: day_4_26_kira
<<set $day_step to 26>>
<<set $playerImage to "images/user/tier_0_2.jpeg">>
I lie on the mattress. Grey sheets. Thin comforter. The apartment is dark except for the second monitor's standby glow and the green LED of the router. The ceiling crack is up there, invisible. The numbers float behind my closed eyes: $363 today. $504 total. 339 peak. 252 followers. The nose is $500 and I'll have it by tomorrow night.

But the numbers fade. The dashboard recedes. And what replaces it, in the dark, on the mattress, is not money.

It's Kira.

The bathrobe.

The image arrives fully formed, preserved in high resolution by a brain that recorded every detail with the obsessive fidelity of a webcam running at 60fps. The white cotton loosely belted. The wet hair dark and heavy against her bare neck. The collarbone exposed where the neckline fell open. The smooth skin of her upper chest, flushed from the shower. The line where the robe ended at mid-thigh and her bare legs began. The way she walked to the kitchen   casual, unhurried, the movement shifting the cotton against her body, the fabric draping and suggesting the topography beneath.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_9.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

The couch. Her thigh across my lap. The kiss that deepened. The "mmnh" against my lips   the involuntary sound, the vibration, the signal from her body that her brain didn't approve. Her chest pressed against my arm through the turtleneck. The shape of her. The specific, imagined-in-detail shape that I felt through two layers of fabric and am now reconstructing in the dark with the focus of an artist working from memory.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_10.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

Her breasts. I felt them. Not directly   through cloth, through cotton, through the incidental geometry of two bodies pressed close on a couch   but I felt them. Small. Firm. The size of   I don't even know the system. Cup sizes. Letters on a scale I've never had reason to learn. B? C? Bigger? She's petite   5'3", slim frame   so they're proportional, which means they could be anything. They felt like enough. They felt like the word "enough" was invented specifically for the thing I felt pressed against my arm.

My hand moves.

Not toward the phone. Not toward the RegenaForm app. Downward. Under the comforter. Under the waistband of the joggers I haven't changed out of. The movement is automatic, the body making decisions the brain already made ten minutes ago in the dark while thinking about cotton robes and collarbone and the sound she makes when she kisses me.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_11.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I think about Kira. Not the stream version of her   not KiraByte with the ring light and the 1,100 viewers. The real one. The one who walks out of a bathroom in a robe like it's nothing. The one who puts her legs in my lap and doesn't flinch when my body responds. The one who looks at me from four inches away and says "your lashes are really long" with the analytical attention of a person who sees everything and the warmth of a person who likes what she sees.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_12.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I think about kissing her. The specific kiss   not the hello or the goodbye but the long one, the one on the couch, her hand on my nape, pulling me down. The way her lips opened against mine and the taste of green tea. The sound. The "mmnh." The vibration transferred from her mouth to mine.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_13.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I think about her chest. The pressure through the fabric. I try to imagine what they look like without the fabric   and I can't, not precisely, because I haven't seen them, but I can approximate. The shape suggested by the bathrobe. The size suggested by the contact. Small but present. Rounded. The skin the same smooth fair tone as her collarbone, as her bare legs, as the skin above the turtleneck that I've been studying for days. I imagine touching them. My hand   the hand with bitten thumbnails   on her breast. The softness. The weight. The way she might react   the gasp, maybe, the gasp I've seen her do on stream when something surprises her, except this would be a different gasp. A private one. The one that lives behind the "mmnh."

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_14.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I think about her lying beside me instead of in her own apartment. On this mattress. On these grey sheets. Her wet hair on my pillow. The bathrobe open. Her eyes without glasses, large and brown and looking up at me the way she looked from four inches away but closer, impossibly close, the closest two people can be.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_16.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

My hand moves. The rhythm is simple. The images are specific. The ceiling crack is invisible above me and the fridge hums its one note and the apartment is dark and I am alone with the memory of a girl who trusts me and the fantasy of a girl I haven't earned and the physical release building in my body the way the viewer count builds during a stream   slowly, then faster, then the peak.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_17.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I think about her saying my name. Not "disaster." Not "Eli." Just the sound of her voice   the real one, not the stream one   saying something soft into the dark space between us. A word. A sound. The "mmnh" expanding into something more.

The peak arrives. The body tenses, arches slightly against the mattress, and then releases   a shudder that moves through me like a wave, carrying with it the tension of the day, the double stream, the performance, the arousal that's been building since the couch, since the bathrobe, since the wet hair and the bare legs and the way she didn't flinch.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_15.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

I lie still. Breathing. The ceiling is dark. The release drains everything   the sexual tension, yes, but also some of the cognitive tension, the spin-cycle of numbers and plans and rationalizations that's been running since I woke up at 8:30. For a few seconds my brain is quiet. Not calculating. Not planning. Just present. A body on a mattress. A person who touched himself thinking about a girl who kissed him.

Normal. Pathetically, beautifully normal.

I clean up with a tissue from the box beside the mattress (the one purchase I made that qualifies as forward-thinking). Settle back. Pull the comforter up.

The numbers try to return. The $363. The nose at $500. The math, the timeline, the RegenaForm app on the phone beside my head. They try to fill the post-orgasmic quiet with their insistent logic.

I let them. For a minute. The nose   after tomorrow's streams, I'll have enough. I'll book the appointment. Walk four blocks. Sit in the chair. Feel the warmth. Walk out with a face that's one step closer to the face reveal, one step closer to telling Kira, one step closer to the life where the numbers support the person instead of replacing him.

But then the numbers fade and what's left is Kira. Her face. Her real face, not the calculated value of it, not the stream metrics, not the bisexuality rationalization. Just her. The freckle near her left eyebrow. The glasses she takes off when she's close. The sound she makes when she kisses me.

Tomorrow I'll modify my nose. Tomorrow I'll stream and earn and grow. Tomorrow the face will change again and the numbers will climb and the loop will continue.

But right now, in the dark, on the grey sheets, in the seconds before sleep   right now I'm just a boy who touched himself thinking about a girl who fell asleep on his shoulder once and walked out of a bathroom in a robe and didn't care that he saw her like that.

That's enough. For right now. That's enough.

I sleep.

End of v0.0.2
